<script>
    import Warning from '$lib/components/markdown/Warning.svelte'
</script>

# Migrating from v0.3.0

<Warning>
v1 is a complete rewrite. There is no incremental upgrade path — you will need to rewrite your DnD setup using the new API.
</Warning>

## The biggest change: no manual boilerplate

In v0.3.0 a basic sortable list required significant boilerplate:

```svelte
<!-- v0.3.0 -->
<script>
    const controller = new DragController();
    const dropPreview = $derived(controller.dropPreview);

    let hiddenId = $state(null);
    const visibleItems = $derived(items.filter(i => i.id !== hiddenId));

    const unsubStart = controller.onDragStart((id) => { hiddenId = id });
    const unsubEnd = controller.onDragEnd(() => { hiddenId = null });

    onDestroy(() => { unsubStart(); unsubEnd(); });
</script>

<DndProvider {controller}>
    <DndDroppable id="list" direction="vertical">
        {#each visibleItems as item, index (item.id)}
            <DndPreview
                containerId="list"
                position={index}
                show={dropPreview?.containerId === 'list' && dropPreview?.position === index}
            />
            <DndDraggable id={item.id}>{item.label}</DndDraggable>
        {/each}
        <DndPreview
            containerId="list"
            position={visibleItems.length}
            show={dropPreview?.containerId === 'list' && dropPreview?.position === visibleItems.length}
        />
    </DndDroppable>
</DndProvider>
```

In v1 all of this is handled automatically:

```svelte
<!-- v1 -->
<script>
    const controller = new DndController();
    controller.onDrop(({ item, target }) => { /* reorder using item.id, target.id, target.position */ });
</script>

<DndProvider {controller}>
    <DndDroppable id="list" direction="vertical">
        {#each items as item, index (item.id)}
            <DndDraggable id={item.id} position={index}>{item.label}</DndDraggable>
        {/each}
    </DndDroppable>
</DndProvider>
```

- `DndPreview` is rendered automatically — remove all manual placements
- The dragged item is hidden automatically via CSS — remove `hiddenId` / `visibleItems`
- No `onDestroy` unsubscribe needed — callbacks are cleaned up automatically

## Controller rename

`DragController` → `DndController`.

```ts
// before
import { DragController } from '@horuse/svelte-dnd'
const controller = new DragController()

// after
import { DndController } from '@horuse/svelte-dnd'
const controller = new DndController()
```

v1 also accepts an optional config object:

```ts
const controller = new DndController({
    scroll: { zoneRatio: 0.3, maxSpeed: 30 },
    preview: { showDelay: 300, collapseDelay: 200 },
    debug: false
})
```

## DndDraggable

`position` is now a **required** prop. Pass the item's index explicitly.

```svelte
<!-- before -->
<DndDraggable id={item.id}>

<!-- after -->
<DndDraggable id={item.id} position={index}>
```

New optional props: `type`.

## DndDroppable

Type filtering moved from `data` to dedicated props:

```svelte
<!-- before -->
<DndDraggable id={item.id} data={{ type: 'task' }}>
<DndDroppable id="list" data={{ accepts: 'task' }}>
<DndDroppable id="list" data={{ accepts: ['task', 'card'] }}>

<!-- after -->
<DndDraggable id={item.id} type="task" position={index}>
<DndDroppable id="list" accepts="task">
<DndDroppable id="list" accepts={['task', 'card']}>
```

New optional props: `mode`, `overlap`.

```svelte
<!-- non-sortable drop zone (e.g. trash, board column) -->
<DndDroppable id="trash" mode="target">
```

## Auto-scroll

In v0.3.0 you had to manually add `data-dnd-scroll` to scrollable elements. In v1 this attribute is gone — auto-scroll activates automatically for any `DndDroppable` that overflows. Remove all `data-dnd-scroll` attributes from your markup.

## DndPreview

`DndPreview` is now internal — **remove all manual placements** from your templates. Do not import or use it directly.

## onDragStart / onDragEnd unsubscribe

In v0.3.0 these returned an unsubscribe function you had to call in `onDestroy`. In v1 callbacks are cleaned up automatically when the controller is destroyed — no `onDestroy` needed.

```ts
// before
const unsub = controller.onDragStart((id) => { ... });
onDestroy(() => unsub());

// after — no onDestroy needed
controller.onDragStart(({ item }) => { ... });
```

## Event callbacks now receive rich objects

All callbacks changed from positional primitives to a single event object:

```ts
// before
controller.onDrop((sourceId, sourceData, targetContainerId, position) => { ... })
controller.onDragStart((itemId) => { ... })
controller.onDragEnd((itemId) => { ... })
controller.onDropCancelled((itemId) => { ... })
controller.onDragOver((containerId, position, prevContainerId) => { ... })

// after
controller.onDrop(({ item, source, target }) => { ... })
controller.onDragStart(({ item, source }) => { ... })
controller.onDragEnd(({ item, source, target, cancelled }) => { ... })
controller.onDropCancelled(({ item, source }) => { ... })
controller.onDragOver(({ item, source, current, previous }) => { ... })
```

`item.id`, `target.id`, and `target.position` replace the old positional `sourceId`, `targetContainerId`, and `position` respectively. Each event also carries `item.data`, `item.type`, `item.element`, plus full `Droppable` entity references on source/target containers.

## New callback: onDropCancelled

Already available in v1 with the new signature:

```ts
controller.onDropCancelled(({ item, source }) => {
    // drag ended without a drop
})
```

## TypeScript

`DragController` type is removed — use `DndController`.

New exports: `DndControllerConfig`, `ScrollConfig`, `PreviewConfig`, `StrategyFactory`, `DndMode`, `DragSource`, `DndItemInfo`, `DndContainerInfo`, `DragStartEvent`, `DropEvent`, `DragEndEvent`, `DragOverEvent`, `DropCancelledEvent`.
